foundation.question_text:
A ball is rolled horizontally off the top of a $20\text{ m}$ cliff at $15\text{ m/s}$. Taking the launch point as the origin and $g=10\text{ m/s}^{2}$, find the time it takes to reach the ground below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\fill[gray!25] (0,0) rectangle (2,3);
\draw (0,3) -- (2,3) -- (2,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (8,0);
\fill (2,3) circle (2pt);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (2,3) -- (3.6,3) node[midway, above] {$15\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[gray] (0,0) -- (-0.7,0);
\draw[gray] (0,3) -- (-0.7,3);
\draw[|<->|] (-0.5,0) -- (-0.5,3) node[midway, left] {$20\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A ball is thrown from the top of a $20\text{ m}$ cliff at $25\text{ m/s}$ at an angle $\theta$ above the horizontal, where $\tan\theta = \dfrac{3}{4}$. Taking the launch point as the origin and $g=10\text{ m/s}^{2}$, find how far from the base of the cliff the ball lands.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta, angles, quotes}
\fill[gray!25] (0,0) rectangle (2,3);
\draw (0,3) -- (2,3) -- (2,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (9,0);
\coordinate (P) at (2,3);
\coordinate (H) at (3.8,3);
\coordinate (V) at (3.28,3.96);
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (H);
\fill (P) circle (2pt);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (P) -- (V) node[pos=1, above right] {$25\text{ m/s}$};
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = H--P--V};
\draw[gray] (0,0) -- (-0.7,0);
\draw[gray] (0,3) -- (-0.7,3);
\draw[|<->|] (-0.5,0) -- (-0.5,3) node[midway, left] {$20\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
